<title>MALAYSIA: Advance Synergy suspension extended.</title>
<headline>Advance Synergy suspension extended.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The suspension of trading in the shares of Advance Synergy Bhd and United Merchant Group Bhd has been extended by four trading days from Tuesday, the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange said on Monday.</p>
<p>The KLSE said in a statement the suspension, in place since April 24, was to finalise a restructuring plan involving the two companies.</p>
<p>The suspension was granted as Advance Synergy was waiting for the central Bank Negara Malaysia's approval for the restructuring, the KLSE said.</p>
<p>&quot;If the company is still not able to make the full announcement on June 6, 1997, the suspension will be automatically lifted by the exchange on June 9, 1997,&quot; the KLSE said.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
